      "id": "botchan-s02-p0004",
      "source_en": "An uninviting dark room just below the staircase was where I was shown into. It was so close and hot a room, like an oven, that I told them to let me have some other room. They said that it was the only room then available, every other room being unfortunately occupied. Thus I was left alone with my bags to perspire in the hot room. Patience was what I had to learn there. Being told to take a bath, I went, jumped in with a good deal of splash, and came out of the tub in a twinkling. I noticed on my way back that many a cool, cozy room was left unoccupied. Impudent rascals! They had basely",
